       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **What was written:** 2550 mg three times daily is 7,650 mg/day.\n- **The limit:** The usual maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg per day in total (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). This order is 3 times that, which risks serious toxicity, including lactic acidosis.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which totals 2,550 mg/day, the max daily dose.\n- **2550 mg/day total**, divided differently.\n- A lower dose, such as 500 mg twice daily or 850 mg twice daily. Metformin is usually started low and increased slowly to limit GI side effects.\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want, and check with your supervising resident or attending. Once you confirm, I'll enter it right away."
